ONE-LINE POSITIONING
"LifeBridge AI is an organ-aware, explainable and human-supervised transplant
coordination platform. It combines configurable organ-specific decision
support with logistics monitoring, fairness analysis and verifiable
auditability, without replacing authorized clinical or allocation decisions."

KEY DESIGN DECISIONS TO JUSTIFY
- Modular monolith instead of microservices: simpler transactions, testing
  and deployment; modules can be split later.
- Normalized organ-aware schema with junction tables, not organ_type
  copied everywhere.
- Versioned immutable organ configs so past recommendations remain
  explainable.
- Eligibility separate from ranking; deterministic, explainable rules
  rather than a black-box model.
- State machine with separation of duties and permission-based access.
- Event-driven logistics; the countdown never decides viability.
- Hash-chained audit with canonical serialization, HMAC, anchoring and
  restricted permissions, and an honest statement of its limits.
- Synthetic data only; fairness metrics are aggregate with stated
  limitations.

